WEBVTT

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:37.630
On August 5th, 1945, in the sixth year of the Second World War,

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.670
a bomb destroyed the Japanese city of Hiroshima.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:51.160
Its stone etched by heat, which reached thousands of degrees,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.060
a monument recorded the passage of the blast,

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:59.810
and burned into the pavement was the silhouette of one of the many who perished on that fateful day.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:14.780
Throughout the world, the reaction of press and public to the advent of atomic power was prompt and varied.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.700
Well, what did you think of that bomb we dropped on the Japs, Mrs. Glenn?

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:27.390
Oh, isn't it terrible? All those people killed. I don't understand it.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:29.980
Well, it's a great triumph for our...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.240
American industrial know-how. Science has overstepped the bower, producing this

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:41.120
diabolical weapon. The public, baffled by talk of protons, neutrons, isotopes, and

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:47.370
isobars, flocked to atomic exhibits in search of understanding. At such exhibits,

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:52.180
the average person was able to learn such basic facts as that the atom is

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:56.340
sub-microscopic in size, and that the forces which hold it together are the

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.580
same as those which keep the universe in balance.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:05.100
around the particles which form the nucleus of the atom other electrically charged particles

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:11.620
called electrons constantly revolve like planets around the sun it is within the nucleus itself

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:20.120
that the cosmic energy is locked to release this energy laboratory machines generating

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:26.440
millions of volts bombard the nucleus of the atom with particles usually neutrons driven at enormous

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:26.940
of speed.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:42.440
If the voltage generated is not sufficiently powerful, the particles are deflected.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:54.490
As the voltage is raised to the proper amount, the particles reach the speed at which they are able to split the nucleus.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.960
It is the sum total of millions of such releases of energy that make up this new...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.700
source of power. But that this type of power will soon become available to the average citizen

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:12.290
is disclaimed by scientists like Harvard's James B. Conant and leading industrial physicists.

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:17.030
That is, I take it, Professor Wheeler, you feel this question of trying to beat the radiation by

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:21.090
shielding is just one of those problems that no matter how much research you did on it looks

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:27.450
insolub. Is that right? The fundamental principles of the process just simply limit us on what we can

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.470
do. Well therefore

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.160
that looks then i take everybody's agreed that the use of this power for automobiles and planes

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:52.490
seems to be out of the question for technical reasons the key to the atom's secrets was first

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:58.510
given to the world in 1905 when the genius albert einstein defined the relation between all matter

00:03:58.510 --> 00:03:59.250
and energy.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.760
his revolutionary theory of special relativity.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.430
Then, in 1919, Lord Rutherford confirmed Einstein's theory

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.130
by smashing the nitrogen atom.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:18.640
By 1934, Italy's Enrico Fermi and Francis Frederick Jolio

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.260
had made substantial progress.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:25.610
Meanwhile, in America, scientists like Arthur H. Compton,

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:29.970
Harold C. Urey, and Ernest O. Lawrence were carrying on intensive research.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:40.630
In 1939, Lisa Meitner, exiled from Germany, computed the results which could be obtained from splitting uranium.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:50.390
In January of the same year, at George Washington University, whose staff had long been alert to developments in atomic research,

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:57.440
scientists from several nations gathered for a routine conference, heard a report of startling significance.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.870
through from Germany, by way of Denmark, that the German physicists, Hahn and Strassmann,

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:12.470
have just verified that the uranium atom under neutron bombardment actually splits into two parts.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:17.090
To the scientists, this dramatic news brought a great sense of urgency.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:23.660
Summoning his assistant, Dr. Merle A. Toove of the Carnegie Institution,

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:29.980
went at once to his laboratory, simultaneously with scientists at Columbia, California, and John...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:36.100
Hopkins, Toove and his colleagues succeeded within 48 hours in checking the reported findings of the

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:45.460
German physicist. Kill the lights. No longer any doubt about it. That uranium is splitting

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:53.740
into at least two big parts. The biggest kicks are nearly a hundred million electron volts.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:59.780
The results verified. Columbia University's Dr. George B. Pegram called these developments to the

00:05:59.780 --> 00:05:59.980
attention.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.900
of the Navy Department in Washington yes yes we'll be very glad to explain to

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:11.880
your people just what the military possibilities of this uranium fission

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:17.730
may prove to be but to the Navy Department these laboratory experiments

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:23.930
seem to be of no immediate importance very interesting doctor keep us informed

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:29.680
Dr. Pigram concentrated on research at Columbia University working under his

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:29.860
Super.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.260
vision were Dr. Leo Szilard and Dr. Fermi, who were laying the groundwork for a chain reaction

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:44.810
in uranium. Encouraged by their successful progress, Szilard discussed with Dr. Einstein

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:50.620
in the summer of 1939 the results of their findings and stressed the urgent need for

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:56.750
action by the U.S. government. Conscious of the disaster which would inevitably follow,

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.970
if Nazi Germany should be the first to succeed in releasing atomic...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:18.880
energy, Dr. Einstein decided to write a personal letter to the president. Within a few days,

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:23.460
the historic Einstein letter was taken to Washington by a New York economist, Alexander

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:28.380
Sachs, who, through close acquaintance with Mr. Roosevelt's advisors, had easy access to

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:28.880
the White House.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:54.920
letter was immediately brought to the attention of the president. Recognizing the critical

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:59.760
significance of Einstein's message, President Roosevelt signed an order appointing the director

00:07:59.760 --> 00:07:59.980
of...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.880
the National Bureau of Standards, Dr. Lyman J. Briggs, as chairman of a special advisory

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:10.760
committee on uranium. After only one meeting, the committee was able to report that an atomic

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:18.650
bomb was a definite possibility. By the following year, the entire U.S. program of uranium

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:24.120
research had been placed under the supervision of Dr. Vannevar Bush, able director of the

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:29.970
Office of Scientific Research and Development. In December 1941, with...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.200
After the United States at war, Dr. Pigram returned from a fact-finding trip to England

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.690
and reported his findings to Dr. Bush.

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.880
The Germans are certainly working on an atomic bomb.

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:44.380
As Harold Urey told you, we learned that they have been receiving the whole output

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:47.020
of the big Norwegian heavy water plant.

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:49.280
They couldn't have been using it for anything else.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.800
What was your impression of British progress?

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:58.900
Chadwick and the other physicists agree entirely with us that given pure uranium-235,

00:08:58.900 --> 00:08:59.520
we

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:06.630
can make a bomb that will work. They are also confident that it'll be practicable to obtain

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:14.340
the uranium-235. But they realize that it will run into a big industrial job. England is

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:21.030
overtaxed at the present time, and the British are all in favor of having a job done on this

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:27.250
side of the water. Well, we're now all fighting the same war. I'm going to see the president

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.970
tomorrow. I'm sure that he will...

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.900
agree that the job has got to be done and that we'll get the support that we need.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:34.920
That's good.

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:35.700
Thank you.

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:41.980
With presidential backing for an all-out research program, contracts were let to a dozen

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:46.440
laboratories for exhaustive study of every method of any hope of success.

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:54.310
In September 1942, on recommendation of Dr. Bush, the U.S. Army Engineer's newly created

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:59.280
Manhattan District, under Major General Leslie R. Groves, was assigned the task of

00:09:59.280 --> 00:09:59.980
expanding the

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.800
laboratory experiments into huge industrial projects.

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:09.140
Meanwhile, at the University of Chicago,

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:12.080
in a secret laboratory set up within the walls

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:15.350
of the stadium squash courts, a dangerous and partly

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:17.270
unpredictable experiment was undertaken.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.650
Dr. Fermi and his assistants, after months

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:25.330
of arduous preparation, achieved the first controlled chain

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.970
reaction in uranium fission.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:45.800
was now cleared for the practical application of atomic power to the nation's war effort.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:52.840
At Oak Ridge, Tennessee, at Hanford, Washington, and at Los Alamos, New Mexico, mammoth plants

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:59.970
were built for the productionable materials and atomic bombs. To staff these...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.020
establishments, thousands of able young scientists and technicians were called

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:04.580
into service.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:18.050
That's O-A-K, Oak Ridge.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:21.580
All right, I'll be there.

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:27.340
Virtually isolated from the outside world, new communities sprang up almost

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:29.970
overnight as top priority materials...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:36.020
and manpower were made available for the secret project. Oak Ridge, Tennessee with 75,000 people

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:43.400
quickly became the fifth largest city in the state. Mobilized to carry out the most formidable

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:48.900
engineering job in history were thousands of the nation's industrial firms of every size and type.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:56.230
To keep the most closely guarded secret of the war, technicians and even scientists were strictly

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:59.450
limited to knowledge of the specific tasks to which they were assigned.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:22.360
Working on seemingly unrelated jobs, many employees were not even sure producing anything.

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:28.010
And few workers had any conception of the fabulous costs involved.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:29.830
Here it is, General.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:41.880
That's the first time I've seen it, but if you don't mind, I wish you'd hold that under it, because after all, there's about $50 million in that test.

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:50.520
Finally, after three years' work and an expenditure of $2 billion, the atomic experts were ready to test their first bomb.

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:59.390
Before, on July 16, 1945, at the Alamogordo Army Air Base in New Mexico,

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:03.780
a small band of military and civilian technicians waited nervously

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:17.580
stretched out on the sand tensely expectant were general groves

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:27.750
dr bush and dr conant in the control shack was dr j oppenheimer

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:29.940
who assisted by dr ira

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.050
and others had directed the making of the bomb itself.

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:35.540
The automatic control's got it now.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:39.520
Rob, this time mistakes are really high.

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:41.880
It's going to work all right, Robert.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:44.420
And I'm sure we'll never be sorry for it.

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:46.660
But in 40 seconds we'll know.

